   "subject": "Using ggplot, it possible to use the stat_function command to plot a  function within a certain range?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Can you specify the range of a function that you want to plot using<br>stat_function?<p>Thanks,<br>David<br></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hF61Dh5MUHEJ",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2010-02-23T05:09:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: Using ggplot, it possible to use the stat_function command to plot a  function within a certain range?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">You can always specify it in the function itself with a little rigging.<div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">n</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">101</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\">x<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> &lt;- </span>seq<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">0</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">2</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">*</span>pi<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>length.out<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>n<span style=\"color:#001b93\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\">df<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> &lt;- </span>data.frame<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>,</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  <span style=\"color:#000000\">y</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">sin</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>) + <span style=\"color:#000000\">rnorm</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">n</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">sd</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">.2</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147);min-height:16px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(185,138,35)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">f</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\"> &lt;- </span>function<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">){</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>[<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span> &lt; <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>]   &lt;- <span style=\"color:#b98a23\">NA</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>[<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span> &gt; <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">5</span>] &lt;- <span style=\"color:#b98a23\">NA</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>suppressWarnings<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>sin<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">))</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\">}</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147);min-height:16px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\">qplot<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>y<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>data<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>df<span style=\"color:#001b93\">) + </span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>stat_function<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>fun<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>f<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>colour<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9c2211\">&#39;red&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>size<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">)</span></div><div><font color=\"#001B93\" face=\"Monaco\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#001B93\" face=\"Monaco\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica\">Otherwise, you could put down another layer with a path, but the above is probably easier.</span></font></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>david.</div></div><div><br><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div>On Feb 22, 2010, at 10:44 PM, daithiquinn wrote:</div><br></div></div></div>"
