    [
     3,
     "<p>On Feb 23, 12:09 am, David Kahle &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david.ka...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; You can always specify it in the function itself with a little rigging.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; n &lt;- 101<br>&gt; x &lt;- seq(0, 2*pi, length.out = n)<br>&gt; df &lt;- data.frame(<br>&gt;    x = x,<br>&gt;    y = sin(x) + rnorm(n, sd = .2)<br>&gt; )<br>&gt;<br>&gt; f &lt;- function(x){<br>&gt;    x[x &lt; 1]   &lt;- NA<br>&gt;    x[x &gt; 5] &lt;- NA<br>&gt;    suppressWarnings(sin(x))<br>&gt;<br>&gt; }<br>&gt;<br>&gt; qplot(x, y, data = df) +<br>&gt;    stat_function(fun = f, colour = &#39;red&#39;, size = 1)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Otherwise, you could put down another layer with a path, but the above  <br>&gt; is probably easier.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Cheers<br>&gt; david.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; On Feb 22, 2010, at 10:44 PM, daithiquinn wrote:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &gt; Can you specify the range of a function that you want to plot using<br>&gt; &gt; stat_function?<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &gt; Thanks,<br>&gt; &gt; David<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &gt; --<br>&gt; &gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2  <br>&gt; &gt; mailing list.<br>&gt; &gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; &gt; To unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br>&gt; &gt; <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; &gt; For more options, visit this group at<br>&gt; &gt;<a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792384053467000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3tMyufIN3nYIjb4VOLKvuk\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br></p>"
